<title>NEW ZEALAND: Horn to leave NZ Treasury for ANZ in Australia.</title>
<headline>Horn to leave NZ Treasury for ANZ in Australia.</headline>
<dateline>WELLINGTON 1996-07-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Secretary to the New Zealand Treasury, Murray Horn, said on Wednesday he would leave Treasury on August 22 to join the ANZ Banking Group in Australia.</p>
<p>Horn has been appointed to the position of General Manager Strategic Planning at ANZ's head office in Melbourne. He will oversee the development of strategic planning as the ANZ Group strengthens its global lines of business.</p>
<p>The State Services Commission will now have the role of selecting a successor to Horn.  </p>
<p>Horn has been Secretary to the Treasury since 1993.</p>
